IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Articles 9, 10 and 11.
-- LAYER 1. Location data other than traffic data (Art 9), exceptions to line identification and location consent (Art 10),
-- automatic call forwarding (Art 11).
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words, NOTHING = not covered (NOTES.md, "Reading a
-- result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Article 9 -- location data other than traffic data`

-- src:103 | Where location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public communications networks or publicly available electronic communications services, can be processed, such data may only be processed when they are made anonymous, or with the consent of the users or subscribers to the extent and for the duration necessary for the provision of a value added service.
@ref Art 9(1) first sentence (src:103) row:A9(1).s1
GIVEN `the data is location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public communications networks or publicly available electronic communications services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the users or subscribers have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for the provision of a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) first sentence the location data may be processed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about location data other than traffic data relating to users or subscribers of public networks and services
        IF NOT `the data is location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public communications networks or publicly available electronic communications services` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the data is made anonymous` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the users or subscribers have consented` AND `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for the provision of a value added service` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such data may only be processed when they are made anonymous, or with the consent of the users or subscribers"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:103 | The service provider must inform the users or subscribers, prior to obtaining their consent, of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed, of the purposes and duration of the processing and whether the data will be transmitted to a third party for the purpose of providing the value added service.
@ref Art 9(1) second sentence (src:103) row:A9(1).s2
GIVEN `the provider is obtaining the consent of the users or subscribers to the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider must inform the users or subscribers before obtaining their consent` MEANS
    IF `the provider is obtaining the consent of the users or subscribers to the processing of location data other than traffic data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prior to obtaining their consent" -- where no consent is being obtained the sentence is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the provider informed the users or subscribers of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informed them of the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informed them of the duration of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informed them whether the data will be transmitted to a third party for the purpose of providing the value added service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider did so prior to obtaining their consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider's duty to inform is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider informed the users or subscribers of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed`
       AND `the provider informed them of the purposes of the processing`
       AND `the provider informed them of the duration of the processing`
       AND `the provider informed them whether the data will be transmitted to a third party for the purpose of providing the value added service`
       AND `the provider did so prior to obtaining their consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The service provider must inform the users or subscribers, prior to obtaining their consent, of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:103 | Users or subscribers shall be given the possibility to withdraw their consent for the processing of location data other than traffic data at any time.
@ref Art 9(1) third sentence (src:103) row:A9(1).s3
GIVEN `the consent was given for the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) third sentence the users or subscribers must be given the possibility to withdraw their consent at any time` MEANS
    IF `the consent was given for the processing of location data other than traffic data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about consent for the processing of location data other than traffic data
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the users or subscribers have the possibility to withdraw their consent at any time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) third sentence the possibility to withdraw the consent at any time is given` MEANS
    IF `the users or subscribers have the possibility to withdraw their consent at any time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be given the possibility to withdraw their consent for the processing of location data other than traffic data at any time"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:104 | Where consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data, the user or subscriber must continue to have the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of temporarily refusing the processing of such data for each connection to the network or for each transmission of a communication.
@ref Art 9(2) (src:104) row:A9(2)
GIVEN `consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2) the user or subscriber must continue to have the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing` MEANS
    IF `consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the user or subscriber has the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing of such data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is for each connection to the network or for each transmission of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2) the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing is as required` MEANS
    IF `the user or subscriber has the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing of such data`
       AND `the possibility uses a simple means`
       AND `the possibility is free of charge`
       AND `the possibility is for each connection to the network or for each transmission of a communication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must continue to have the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of temporarily refusing the processing of such data"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:105 | Processing of location data other than traffic data in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2 must be restricted to persons acting under the authority of the provider of the public communications network or publicly available communications service or of the third party providing the value added service, and must be restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of providing the value added service.
@ref Art 9(3) (src:105) row:A9(3)
GIVEN `the processing is in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the provider of the public communications network or publicly available communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the third party providing the value added service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of providing the value added service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3) the processing of the location data is restricted as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2" -- processing that is not in accordance with them is outside the paragraph's words
        IF NOT `the processing is in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to persons acting under the authority of the provider of the public communications network or publicly available communications service or of the third party providing the value added service" -- FORK F14: "must be restricted to" read as closing the persons
        IF (NOT `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the provider of the public communications network or publicly available communications service`) AND (NOT `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the third party providing the value added service`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of providing the value added service"
        IF NOT `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of providing the value added service` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 10 -- exceptions`

-- src:108 | Member States shall ensure that there are transparent procedures governing the way in which a provider of a public communications network and/or a publicly available electronic communications service may override:
@ref Art 10 chapeau (src:108) row:A10.chapeau
GIVEN `there is a procedure governing the way in which the provider may override` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the procedure is transparent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10 the Member State has ensured transparent procedures governing the override` MEANS
    IF `there is a procedure governing the way in which the provider may override` AND `the procedure is transparent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States shall ensure that there are transparent procedures governing the way in which a provider of a public communications network and/or a publicly available electronic communications service may override"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:109 | the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification, on a temporary basis, upon application of a subscriber requesting the tracing of malicious or nuisance calls.
@ref Art 10(a) first sentence (src:109) row:A10(a).s1
GIVEN `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the override is on a temporary basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the override is upon application of a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber requests the tracing of malicious or nuisance calls` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(a) first sentence the provider may override the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification` MEANS
    IF `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification`
       AND `the override is on a temporary basis`
       AND `the override is upon application of a subscriber`
       AND `the subscriber requests the tracing of malicious or nuisance calls`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the override is named for a temporary override upon a subscriber's application to trace malicious or nuisance calls; outside that the sentence is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:109 | In this case, in accordance with national law, the data containing the identification of the calling subscriber will be stored and be made available by the provider of a public communications network and/or publicly available electronic communications service;
@ref Art 10(a) second sentence (src:109) row:A10(a).s2
GIVEN `the provider has overridden the elimination of calling line identification under paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the storing and making available is in accordance with national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(a) second sentence the data identifying the calling subscriber will be stored and made available by the provider` MEANS
    IF `the provider has overridden the elimination of calling line identification under paragraph (a)` AND `the storing and making available is in accordance with national law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in accordance with national law" -- the national law is not among the sources; where the storing is not shown to be in accordance with it, the text does not answer
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:110 | the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification and the temporary denial or absence of consent of a subscriber or user for the processing of location data, on a per-line basis for organisations dealing with emergency calls and recognised as such by a Member State, including law enforcement agencies, ambulance services and fire brigades, for the purpose of responding to such calls.
@ref Art 10(b) (src:110) row:A10(b)
GIVEN `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification, or of the temporary denial or absence of consent for the processing of location data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the override is on a per-line basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organisation deals with emergency calls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organisation is recognised as such by a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the override is for the purpose of responding to emergency calls` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(b) the provider may override for the organisation` MEANS
    IF `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification, or of the temporary denial or absence of consent for the processing of location data`
       AND `the override is on a per-line basis`
       AND `the organisation deals with emergency calls`
       AND `the organisation is recognised as such by a Member State`
       AND `the override is for the purpose of responding to emergency calls`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including law enforcement agencies, ambulance services and fire brigades" does not close the list; an organisation that is not recognised by a Member State is outside the words
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 11 -- automatic call forwarding`

-- src:113 | Member States shall ensure that any subscriber has the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of stopping automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal.
@ref Art 11 (src:113) row:A11
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the forwarding is automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11 the subscriber must have the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber` AND `the forwarding is automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a subscriber and automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the subscriber has the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11 the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding is as required` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber has the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding` AND `the possibility uses a simple means` AND `the possibility is free of charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any subscriber has the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of stopping automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE
